# Hits are pinned to the `for` keyword line.
# Known non-hit shapes: I used arithmetically, a write A[I] := .. or
# A[I].F := .., I read after the loop, A[I+1], downto, a different container
# than the bound, a start other than 0, a body that mutates the container (Delete, Add,
# SetLength).
index-loop-to-for-in 15
index-loop-to-for-in 23
index-loop-to-for-in 33
index-loop-to-for-in 39
!index-loop-to-for-in 47
!index-loop-to-for-in 55
!index-loop-to-for-in 63
!index-loop-to-for-in 71
!index-loop-to-for-in 80
!index-loop-to-for-in 88
!index-loop-to-for-in 96
!index-loop-to-for-in 104
!index-loop-to-for-in 112
!index-loop-to-for-in 123
!index-loop-to-for-in 134
